A||||5||Mark Matthews||Another tire question||||5||
Z||000000||Mark Matthews||12-08-2001||01:33 PM||||Okay, Right now I have the 215/60 R15's on my car.  The FR is totally shot.  I just wanna replace the front two with used for right now till I can go thru everything.  The shops in town only have 205's and 235's.  Which size would work better, a keep my speedo close to the same?  Or is the speedo off the back wheels?  Thanks!  I'd like to get them today.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!  ;)||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-08-2001||01:44 PM||||The speedo gets it's signal from the tranny end of the beast.  Assuming the tires are 60 series,tere will be no effect on the speedo. The 205/235 signifies tread width. The 205's will be easier to steer, especially with any significant snowfall you may receive in LV.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Gary<BR><p>[This message has been edited by FieroBUZZ (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Oreif||12-08-2001||02:52 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroBUZZ:<BR><B>The speedo gets it's signal from the tranny end of the beast.  Assuming the tires are 60 series,tere will be no effect on the speedo. The 205/235 signifies tread width. The 205's will be easier to steer, especially with any significant snowfall you may receive in LV.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Gary<P><BR>[This message has been edited by FieroBUZZ (edited 12-08-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Go with the 205's. The 235's are taller tires. The way the numbers work is:<BR>205 = width<BR>60 = 60% of the width makes up the sidewall.<P>So if you use a 235 tire 60% of the width is sidewall. This makes the sidewall taller.<BR>205mm width has a 123mm sidewall<BR>235mm width has a 141mm sidewall<BR>18mm (or 1.8cm) is about .6 inch difference.<BR>So a 235 tire is over 1/2" taller than a 205 and just over 1/4" taller than the 215's on the car. If you want the 235's, put them in the rear and the 215's up front.<P>Speedo will be off by 2.3%. So at 100mph you'll really be going 102.3mph. At 50mph you'll really be going 51.15mph.<P>Providing of course how acurate the speedo is originally.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">             <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||12-08-2001||03:26 PM||||The  Fieros with the 15" wheels came stock with 205's on the front, and 215's on the back.<P>I'd go with the 205's<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark Matthews||12-08-2001||04:28 PM||||Thanks guys, found some cheap used 205's for the front for $60 mounted and balanced.  They're just till I get everything checked out for the Echeck.  I don't want a fail on the title.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks guys!<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!  ;)||||reg||1
